TEHORA est présentement à la recherche **des techniciens en soutien informatique à distance** possédant une expérience en assistance aux utilisateurs, diagnostic d’incidents et soutien bureautique dans des environnements technologiques complexes. Ces ressources participeront aux opérations du centre d’assistance du ministère et assureront le premier niveau de soutien aux utilisateurs partout au Québec.


Sans être exhaustifs, voici les services et livrables que devra fournir la personne retenue :

* Recevoir et traiter les appels, courriels et demandes de service des utilisateurs;
* Diagnostiquer et résoudre les incidents informatiques à distance;
* Assurer le soutien aux outils Microsoft 365 (Outlook, Teams, Word, Excel, SharePoint);
* Effectuer le soutien des environnements VPN et télétravail;
* Administrer les comptes utilisateurs dans Active Directory et Entra ID;
* Documenter les interventions dans l’outil GSTI du client;
* Effectuer l’escalade des incidents vers les équipes spécialisées lorsque requis;
* Participer à l’amélioration continue des processus de soutien;
* Maintenir un haut niveau de qualité de service à la clientèle;
* Participer aux rencontres de coordination et aux activités de transfert de connaissances.



**Requirements**  

* Détenir un DEC ou une AEC en informatique et un minimum d’une (1\) année d’expérience pertinente;
* Ou détenir un DEP en informatique et un minimum de trois (3\) années d’expérience pertinente;
* Posséder une expérience en soutien aux utilisateurs dans un environnement corporatif;
* Maîtriser Microsoft 365 et l’environnement Windows;
* Posséder des connaissances en Active Directory et Entra ID;
* Posséder des connaissances en réseautique TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP et Wi\-Fi;
* Posséder d’excellentes aptitudes en service à la clientèle;
* Faire preuve d’autonomie, de rigueur et d’un excellent sens des priorités;
* Communiquer clairement en français, tant à l’oral qu’à l’écrit;
* Être admissible à une vérification de sécurité gouvernementale.

 **Benefits**  

* Du télétravail et de la flexibilité pour s’adapter à vos obligations familiales
* Une culture entrepreneuriale favorisant la créativité et l’innovation
* Horaires flexibles (selon le type de contrat de travail)
* Congés en cas de maladie et à l’occasion d’événements familiaux
* Outils informatiques adaptés
* Espace de travail épanouissant et motivant
* Initiatives sociales et environnementales
* Programme d’apprentissage en milieu de travail
* Cheminement de carrière


SALAIRE
Le salaire sera calculé sur la base du taux horaire moyen correspondant à votre profil.


LIEU DE TRAVAIL
Québec – Télétravail avec présence occasionnelle.


POURQUOI SE JOINDRE À TEHORA ?
TEHORA est une firme québécoise multidisciplinaire reconnue pour l’excellence de ses services professionnels, de nature technique et de gestion de projets à l’échelle nationale et internationale. Notre mission est d’accompagner nos clients dans la concrétisation de leurs projets par l’excellence de notre savoir\-faire et de notre créativité.


Depuis sa création en 2017, notre équipe de professionnels connaît une croissance exponentielle en répondant aux besoins importants en gestion de projets multidisciplinaires, dans le domaine des transports, du génie civil, du TI et plus.


Nos collaborateurs travaillent sur des mandats aussi bien à l’interne que chez des clients d’envergure.


TEHORA se distingue par sa culture d’entreprise, axée sur le bonheur de ses employés et la diversité.


Chez TEHORA, chaque collaborateur est un membre important de l’équipe qui contribue à notre succès collectif. Nos membres ont la flexibilité requise pour avoir un équilibre entre le travail et leur vie privée, tout en menant une carrière enrichissante.


Nous offrons un environnement de travail motivant. La diversité des projets, la grande autonomie et l’interaction directe avec les clients sont appréciées. Une telle proximité est possible en raison de notre structure organisationnelle horizontale, qui se traduit par des relations de confiance et une communication efficace entre notre équipe et les clients.

***Data. Discovery. Better Health.***


***ICES is a world\-leading health research and analytics institute. With a wealth of data and analytic expertise, we create trusted evidence that has changed health policy and practice and helps ensure better health for all.***


***Ready to discover more with us? Join our outstanding, collaborative team where your skills, knowledge and curiosity are valued and can change the future of health care.***

 **At ICES, we recognize what matters most to our employees. Some of the great benefits of working at ICES include:**


* Flexible work arrangements
* Competitive Compensation
* Comprehensive Benefits Program
* HOOPP Pension Plan (Defined Pension)
* Employee Assistance Program and Dialogue Well Being Program
* Generous vacation, float and caregiver days for all employees
* Education Fund and Dedicated Education Days
* Holiday Closure
* Perkopolis Employee Discount Program




**Introduction:**





ICES is seeking a Technical Support Analyst to join our Technology department. The Technical Support Analyst is responsible for providing comprehensive end\-user technical support and fulfilling service requests to ensure the smooth operation of IT services. Reporting to the Manager of the IT Service Desk, this role plays a critical part in enhancing user satisfaction and productivity by resolving technical issues efficiently and effectively, thereby contributing to the overall success of the organization’s IT initiatives.

 **Responsibilities of the position include, but may not be limited to:**

 **First Level Support and Incident Management:**


* Accountable for providing first\-level support via email, phone, Teams chat, or onsite to address user inquiries and technical issues. Responsible for ensuring all requests are resolved within established service level agreement (SLA) by applying strong communication and problem\-solving skills to deliver timely, effective solutions that enhance user satisfaction and productivity;
* Perform Identity and Access Management (IAM) tasks, including onboarding new user accounts, validating, and updating access permissions, and offboarding user accounts to ensure proper security and compliance across the organization;
* Record and document all interactions through ITSM platform, ensuring accurate tracking of incidents and requests. This involves using organizational skills and clear communication to maintain detailed records, which facilitate effective follow\-up and trend analysis, ultimately improving service delivery;
* Conduct regular reviews of incident reports to identify recurring issues and areas for improvement. This involves utilizing analytical skills to interpret data trends and collaborating with team members to develop strategies that enhance service delivery and reduce the frequency of common problems;
* Responsible for managing endpoint assets by provisioning and configuring laptops, maintaining, and updating software packages, and overseeing the administration of security policies to ensure all devices comply with ICES standards. This is achieved by utilizing technical expertise and familiarity with hardware and software systems to diagnose and resolve issues efficiently;
* Enhance automation workflows by developing, optimizing, and maintaining scripting language including PowerShell to streamline system operations, reduce manual intervention and improve consistency across environments;
* Maintain asset inventory for procurement, troubleshooting and repairs, and decommission.



**Knowledge base Management and Project Initiatives:**


* Create, review, and update the Service Desk knowledge base articles to support service delivery, user feedback, and Technology updates. This involves writing and editing skills to ensure that documentation is clear, accurate, and accessible, enabling both users and support staff to find solutions quickly. This requires collaboration with team members to ensure that all documentation reflects current practices and procedures, enhancing the overall efficiency of the IT support team;
* Lead support\-related initiatives by overseeing the planning, execution and operation integration of new processes, tools, and service improvements.


**Orientation and Training:**


* Provide orientation and training to new staff on IT procedures, laptop management, and best practices. This involves utilizing instructional skills and knowledge of IT systems to ensure that staff are equipped with the necessary tools and information to effectively use technology in their roles. Developing training materials and resources that clearly explain IT processes is essential, as it ensures that all new staff have access to comprehensive guidance and can operate independently;
* Facilitate ongoing training sessions for existing staff to keep them updated on new technologies and IT procedures. This requires strong presentation skills and the ability to engage participants, ensuring that all team members are informed and capable of utilizing IT resources effectively.


**Other:**


* Other duties as may be assigned within the scope of this position.




**Knowledge, skills, and abilities:**


**Minimum Required Education, Years of Experience, and Certifications/Professional Designations:**


* College Diploma in Information Technology or equivalent.;
* 2 years of technical support experience in Windows/Mac OS.;
* IT industry certificates such as ITIL Foundation.



**Minimum Required Position\-Specific Knowledge and Technical Skills:**


* Proficiency in hardware configuration, upgrade, troubleshooting, and repair (desktops, laptops, and peripherals);
* Experience working with IT Service Management tools, including BMC TrackIT;
* Experienced with Server Administration and Azure Tools including Active Directory/Entra ID, Group Policy Management, Citrix Management and VMWare;
* Experience in EndPoint Management including Intune and SCCM, application management using PMPC, Vulnerability Manage

Your Next Challenge at Techso


Are you looking to go beyond execution and truly contribute to the technical decisions behind a project?


Techso is looking for a Senior Full Stack .NET Developer to help design and develop digital solutions used by our clients across Canada.


In this role, you'll have the opportunity to work on a variety of projects, contribute to architectural decisions, mentor less experienced developers, and help improve our development practices.


Who We Are


Founded in Montreal in 2014, Techso helps organizations accelerate their digital transformation through three areas of expertise:


IT Infrastructure Management;


Custom Application Development;


Product Lifecycle Management (PLM).


Our team works with recognized clients across a variety of industries, including aerospace, automotive, finance, events, and watchmaking.


At Techso, we value the quality of our projects and relationships over volume. Our core values—Fun, Trust, Efficiency, and Quality—guide both the way we work with our clients and how we collaborate as colleagues.


What You'll Do


**Depending on the projects assigned to you, you will:**  
Design and develop new applications;


Enhance existing solutions by adding new features, resolving issues, and providing ongoing maintenance;


Contribute to the design of innovative solution architectures that meet client needs;


Write and maintain technical and functional specifications;


Estimate the development effort required for new solutions and enhancements;


Participate in production deployments and support change management activities;


Ensure code quality through code reviews, unit testing, and software development best practices;


Contribute to the continuous improvement of Agile practices, continuous integration, and automated deployment processes;


Participate in pre-sales activities, including effort estimation and technology assessments;


Share your expertise and mentor junior team members;


Stay current with emerging technologies and industry best practices;


Collaborate with multidisciplinary Agile Scrum teams.


The Profile We're Looking For


**You have:**  
A bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field;


At least six years of experience with Microsoft .NET technologies (C#, ASP.NET, Web API);


Strong experience with front-end development using React, Angular, or Vue.js;


Excellent knowledge of relational databases, SQL, and tools such as Entity Framework;


A solid understanding of DevOps practices and continuous integration and deployment environments;


Experience working in an Agile and collaborative environment;


Good knowledge of Linux and Windows environments;


The flexibility to travel within the Montreal area to meet client needs;


The ability to communicate professionally in both French and English, as you will collaborate with colleagues and clients located across Quebec and Canada;


Strong interpersonal skills, autonomy, and a collaborative mindset.


Nice to Have


Experience with Azure DevOps;


Knowledge of NoSQL databases;


Experience with ETL processes;


Knowledge of other programming languages such as Java, PHP, Node.js, or Python;


Experience with MAUI, Xamarin, or Telerik;


Experience in solution architecture, mentoring, or technical pre-sales.


You don't need to master every one of these technologies. Above all, we're looking for an experienced, curious professional who can adapt to a variety of projects.


What Techso Offers


Challenging and diverse projects with recognized clients across Canada.


A flexible hybrid work model adapted to project and client needs.


Bright offices in the heart of Old Montreal, featuring a rooftop terrace.


Complimentary breakfast, snacks, and coffee available at the office.


A vibrant social and sports club, fully sponsored by Techso.


International mobility opportunities through our consultant mobility program.


The opportunity to contribute beyond client projects by participating in internal initiatives that help shape the company's future.


A collaborative community of experts that encourages knowledge sharing and professional development.


Comprehensive private group insurance tailored to your needs.


A culture built on Fun, Trust, Efficiency, and Quality.

